String scannerPage(){return R"HTML(<!doctype html><html><head><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover"><meta name="theme-color" content="#08111f"><title>T1N Scanner</title><style>
:root{--bg:#07101c;--panel:#0d1928;--line:#24374f;--text:#eef6ff;--muted:#8ea2ba;--blue:#2b7fff;--green:#2fc477;--red:#ef5b62}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font:15px system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,sans-serif}.wrap{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:14px 14px 90px}.top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;align-items:center;padding:5px 0 14px}.brand{font-size:22px;font-weight:850}.sub{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}.statusDot{width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;display:inline-block;background:#64748b;margin-right:7px}.statusDot.ok{background:var(--green);box-shadow:0 0 12px #2fc47788}.statusDot.bad{background:var(--red)}.nav{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:7px;background:#091523;border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px;border-radius:14px;position:sticky;top:6px;z-index:10}.nav button{background:transparent;color:var(--muted);border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:10px 4px;font-weight:750}.nav button.on{background:#173252;color:#fff}.view{display:none}.view.on{display:block}.hero{margin:12px 0;background:linear-gradient(145deg,#10233a,#0c1725);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;padding:16px}.heroRow{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start}.moduleName{font-size:23px;font-weight:850}.badge{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;padding:5px 9px;color:#b9c8d8;font-size:12px}.actions{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:14px}button{border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:10px 13px;background:#24415f;color:#fff;font-weight:800;cursor:pointer}.primary{background:var(--blue)!important}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(165px,1fr));gap:9px;margin:10px 0}.metric{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:13px;min-height:96px}.metric.stale{opacity:.48}.metric .label{color:#9eb0c5;font-size:12px;min-height:30px}.metric .value{font-size:27px;font-weight:850;line-height:1.15;margin-top:4px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.metric .unit{font-size:12px;color:#8296ad;margin-left:3px}.sectionTitle{font-size:17px;font-weight:850;margin:18px 2px 8px}.moduleGrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:10px}.module{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:15px;padding:14px}.module.active{border-color:#3b82f6;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px #3b82f633}.module h3{margin:0 0 5px}.pin{font-size:24px;font-weight:850;color:#8dc0ff}.note{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px;line-height:1.45}.faultBox{white-space:pre-wrap;background:#050b12;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:13px;padding:13px;min-height:130px;font:13px ui-monospace,monospace;color:#dce9f7}.notice{border:1px solid #6b5229;background:#251d11;color:#ffd999;border-radius:12px;padding:10px 12px;margin:10px 0}.error{color:#ff9ca2;font-size:13px;margin-top:8px}.footerLink{display:block;text-align:center;margin-top:22px;color:#91bfff;text-decoration:none}.tiny{font-size:11px;color:#71869e}@media(max-width:560px){.wrap{padding:10px 10px 80px}.nav button{font-size:12px}.moduleName{font-size:20px}.metric .value{font-size:24px}}
</style></head><body><div class="wrap"><div class="top"><div><div class="brand">T1N Scanner</div><div class="sub">2003 Sprinter diagnostic scanner · <span id="fw">...</span></div></div><div class="badge"><span id="dot" class="statusDot"></span><span id="linkState">Disconnected</span></div></div>
<div class="nav"><button class="on" data-v="overview">Overview</button><button data-v="live">Live Data</button><button data-v="faults">Fault Codes</button><button data-v="modules">Modules</button></div>
<section id="overview" class="view on"><div class="hero"><div class="heroRow"><div><div class="sub">ACTIVE MODULE</div><div id="moduleName" class="moduleName">Engine / CR2</div><div class="sub">Address <span id="addr">0x12</span> · OBD diagnostic pin <b id="pin">7</b></div></div><span id="pollBadge" class="badge">Live data off</span></div><div id="err" class="error"></div><div class="actions"><button id="connectBtn" class="primary" onclick="connectActive()">Connect</button><button onclick="showView('modules')">Choose Module</button></div></div><div class="sectionTitle">Key data</div><div id="keyCards" class="cards"></div><div class="note">Values fade when they have not been refreshed recently. Open Live Data for every available value from the selected module.</div></section>
<section id="live" class="view"><div class="sectionTitle">Live Data · <span id="liveModule">...</span></div><div class="actions"><button class="primary" onclick="pollOn()">Start live data</button><button onclick="pollOff()">Stop</button></div><div id="allCards" class="cards"></div></section>
<section id="faults" class="view"><div class="sectionTitle">Fault Codes · <span id="faultModule">...</span></div><div class="actions"><button class="primary" onclick="readDtc()">Read fault codes</button></div><div id="absDtcNote" class="notice" style="display:none">ABSBR901 fault definitions are decoded, but its CBF did not expose a verified fault-read request. This build will not guess or transmit an unverified ABS fault-memory command.</div><div id="faultText" class="faultBox">No fault-code read yet.</div><div class="note" style="margin-top:8px">Fault clearing and raw commands stay in Advanced so normal scanner use remains read-only.</div></section>
<section id="modules" class="view"><div class="sectionTitle">Control Modules</div><div class="moduleGrid"><div id="mod0" class="module"><h3>Engine · CR2</h3><div class="pin">OBD pin 7</div><div class="note">Address 0x12 · OM612 common-rail ECU. Connection and live data are already verified on this van.</div><div class="actions"><button class="primary" onclick="selectModule(0)">Use Engine</button></div></div><div id="mod1" class="module"><h3>ABS · ABSBR901</h3><div class="pin">OBD pin 9</div><div class="note">Address 0x34 · wheel speeds, brake switches, pump feedback, valve feedback and ABS supply voltage from the decoded CBF.</div><div class="actions"><button class="primary" onclick="selectModule(1)">Use ABS</button></div></div><div id="mod2" class="module"><h3>Transmission · EGS52</h3><div class="pin">OBD pin 11</div><div class="note">Address 0x20 · gear, selector position, transmission temperature, turbine/output RPM, vehicle speed and voltage.</div><div class="actions"><button class="primary" onclick="selectModule(2)">Use Transmission</button></div></div></div><div class="notice">The ESP32 K-line interface must be electrically connected to the OBD pin shown for the module. Software changes the diagnostic address, but cannot physically move the K-line wire between pins 7, 9 and 11.</div></section>
